# config/wedge-alarm - shared active-alert channels for serious supervision
# failures, including an away-mode injection wedge and the supervisor
# watchdog's aged durable-wake alarm. Copy this into a local, gitignored
# config/wedge-alarm and edit. One channel directive per non-empty, non-comment
# line; every listed non-off channel fires, best-effort.
#
# Directives:
#   off              position-independent kill switch: disable every active
#                    notification (caller-owned durable markers and any
#                    caller-specific visual signal remain)
#   auto | default   platform default: macOS -> osascript; other platforms have
#                    no built-in OS channel (configure a command: line instead)
#   osascript        macOS Notification Center banner (backend-independent)
#   herdr            herdr UI notification (herdr notification show)
#   command:<cmd>    run <cmd> via `sh -c`; the alarm summary is passed as $1 and
#                    on stdin, so it can reach a phone/pager while you are away
#
# An ABSENT config/wedge-alarm behaves as `auto` (default-on on macOS): the
# alert exists so a serious supervision failure is never silent.
#
# Example: a macOS banner plus a push to a phone via ntfy.sh, so a supervision
# failure reaches you even away from the machine.
osascript
command: curl -fsS -H "Title: firstmate supervision alert" -d "$1" https://ntfy.sh/replace-with-your-topic
